n When to apply, labelled \"Eric's baseline:\". Department names: Athletic Performance, Athletic Medicine, Applied Performance. Plain style, no em dashes. Use commas, colons and parentheses.\n56:## Scope and output","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d2ea452f-efc4-4e29-8fad-51fa851aa6c6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:20:40.141Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"      60 docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md\n1:# Atomization brief (shared by every Flint ingest agent)\n3:Read this whole file before writing anything. It holds the rules the Harries review taught (2026-09-26: 25 of 35 files needed fixes). The review gate will check every rule here.\n5:## Schema\n11:## Voices: label every one\n14:- **Eric's views** (from `docs/method-baseline.md` or his reviews) are prefixed \"Eric's baseline:\" or \"Eric's review:\".\n16:- **Nothing unlabeled that the author did not say.** The most common failures: a judgment from Eric's review written as if the author said it; a mechanism the author never gave presented as \"why it works\" (write \"The author gives no mechanism. Inference: ...\"); an invented example.\n18:## Lessons from the Supertraining Chapter 1 review (2026-09-26: 30 FIX, 1 NO-GO of 41)\n23:- **No mechanism the source does not give.** About a dozen \"Why it works\" sections supplied physiology the book never states. Label it \"Inference:\" or leave it out.\n26:## Lessons from the 2026-09-27 review wave (Supertraining Ch2-3, Issurin Ch3, Bondarchuk, Evans, Old Bull)\n32:- **No review history in entries.** \"Prior version\", \"corrected from a NO-GO finding\" and similar belong in `staging/fixes_*_applied.md`, never in the entry body.\n34:- **Section headers use the vault form** `**What it is** —` (with the em dash). Do not add suffixes such as \": mandatory\". Em dashes are banned only in titles and body text. Never wrap a `[[wikilink]]` across lines.\n36:## Evidence\n43:## Confidence\n48:## Dedup and converge\n52:## Baylor context\n54:Read `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\workt