{"parentUuid":"8ed8665e-1336-4f2a-ba71-c8518dbdf7b2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a943b4c4c92ae7c73","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffcewHQvhsdNuY2WyFYW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** One fix is still needed, in one file. The other 18 entries can be promoted as they stand.\n\n**Counts:** 18 GO, 1 FIX, 0 NO-GO.\n\n**The one fix:** in `claim--implement-mass-for-speed-strength-keep-technique-and-size-per-athlete.md`, the When NOT section says \"only the shot and baseball data fit\" a stay-close-to-competition-mass rule. The baseball part is wrong. Round 1 suggested that wording and the fixer copied it in.\n- The page (PDF 276 / p.265) gives a 57 g light ball and a 184 g heavy ball against a regulation ball of about 148 g. The light ball is 61% under regulation, as far off as the counterexamples the same sentence lists. The heavy ball is 24% over.\n- That study measured precision transfer, not whether a closer mass works better.\n- Fix: say only the shot data fit. The exact replacement text is in the report.\n\n**What held up:**\n- **All 7 round-1 FIX entries:** every flagged problem is gone. Six are now GO; the implement-mass entry is the FIX above.\n- **Newton II physics:** correct line by line.\n  - The impulse of the net external force equals m(v_final - v_initial).\n  - The book's m.ΔV equals that only when the body starts from rest.\n  - Net propulsive impulse is measured from zero velocity at the bottom of the countermovement.\n  - The constant-gravity projectile example now correctly answers the book's sentence.\n  - `proven` covers only the identity.\n- **The fixer's five disagreements with round 1:** each is backed by the page.\n- **Links:** every wikilink in the 19 files resolves. The two old slugs appear nowhere in staging entries, scope files or the vault, only in the round-1 review and the fix log.\n- **Format:** all 19 files have the six headers once each, no em dashes outside headers, no wrapped links and no review-history wording.\n\n**GO entries spot-checked (6 of 11)**, against the page images:\n- `principle--speed-strength-strength-endurance-and-speed-endurance-are-independent-qualities`\n- `heuristic--analytical-synthetic-and-multifaceted-preparation-suit-only-early-training`\n- `framework--apre-autoregulating-progressive-resistance-exercise` (every cell of Table 5.2)\n- `case-study--arm-throw-height-after-barbell-press-tonic-work` (all 18 cells of Table 5.3, with the percentages recomputed)\n- `heuristic--cyclic-vs-acyclic-speed-strength-tempo-rest-and-fatigue`\n- `case-study--alternate-leg-bounding-with-thigh-cuffs-for-sprinters`\n\nI also re-checked the speed-strength loading entry, which the fixer edited; it is GO.\n\nThree small wording issues are listed in the report as optional; none blocks promotion. Pages 266, 273 and 275 were checked from the extracted text only, not the page images.\n\nThe report is at `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5a_opus_round2.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6092,"cache_read_input_tokens":154659,"output_tokens":1116,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":46},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6092},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1116,"cache_read_input_tokens":154659,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6092,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cffceorvk9C4nN7jffMpE","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b2328919-4ce2-428c-92d4-d3fa